### Go ###
# Binaries for programs and plugins
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib

# Test binary, built with `go test -c`
*.test

# Output of the go coverage tool, specifically when used with LiteIDE
*.out

# Dependency directories (remove the comment below to include it)
# vendor/

### Go Patch ###
/vendor/
/Godeps/

### Vim ###
# Swap
[._]*.s[a-v][a-z]
[._]*.sw[a-p]
[._]s[a-rt-v][a-z]
[._]ss[a-gi-z]
[._]sw[a-p]

# Session
Session.vim
Sessionx.vim

# Temporary
.netrwhist
*~

# Auto-generated tag files
tags

# Persistent undo
[._]*.un~

# Coc configuration directory
.vim

# End of https://www.gitignore.io/api/go,vim

*.log
transceiver-exporter

# GoReleaser build output
/dist/

# zensical local build output. The published site is built independently by the
# rknightion/m7kni-net-site hub from docs/ + docs.toml.
/site/

# Injected by the m7kni.io hub at build time — never commit these.
# The hub copies its own SEO template, brand stylesheet and fonts into a clone
# and generates zensical.toml from docs.toml. A tracked copy here is drift, and
# is exactly what the manifest model exists to prevent.
/zensical.toml
docs/overrides/
docs/stylesheets/brand.css
docs/assets/project-icon.svg
docs/assets/project-icon-solid.svg
docs/assets/social-card.png
docs/assets/social-card.svg
docs/fonts/

# Superpowers scratch (specs/plans/audits) — never committed
docs/superpowers/

# Only the shared Claude Code config is tracked: settings.json and hooks/, so the Backlog.md guard
# (bare --notes/--plan replaces a section silently; hand-edited task markdown loses one at exit 0)
# applies to anyone working in this repo. Everything else under .claude/ is per-machine state —
# worktrees, scheduler locks, settings.local.json.
.claude/*
!.claude/settings.json
!.claude/hooks/
